{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789237449,"nonce":"pUDKnPVfkBvf5XT4Ysy5yu9IIjo=","title":"Cranelift horizontal add emits iadd_pairwise on i64x2, which the verifier rejects","message":"The auto-vectorizer turns an i64 sum loop into an i64x2 reduction, and\nVectorHorizontalReduce in cranelift_backend.rs lowers an integer Add on\nI32X4 or I64X2 through an `iadd_pairwise` tree. Cranelift defines\n`iadd_pairwise` for lanes of at most 32 bits, so every function holding\nan i64x2 reduction fails IR verification and is skipped; the caller then\nreports \"Function not found\".\n\nReproducer (Python frontend): `xs = [x for x in range(5)]; print(sum(xs))`.\nThe list-sum library function is `let s = 0; while i \u003c n { s = s + xs[i] }`\nover i64. A literal list did not show it because the trip count was known\nand the loop was not vectorized.\n\nFix: pairwise only on I32X4; I64X2 takes the serial extractlane chain.","files":null}]}